From: aria2-cross <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] configure: do not link the Linux system libraries on iOS

EXTRALIBS gains -lpthread -ldl -lrt for a static build on any host that is
not mingw, msvc or darwin. arm64-apple-ios is none of those, so it took the
Linux branch and the link failed with

    ld: library 'rt' not found

iOS is Darwin: pthread, dlopen and clock_gettime all live in libSystem, and
there is no librt, libdl or libpthread to link against. Listing ios beside
darwin is the whole fix.

Both files are patched, and that part is not optional. The release tarball
ships configure already generated, and configure is what actually runs --
patching configure.ac alone changes a file nothing reads, because the
generated copy still holds the old case statement. Regenerating it instead
would need autoconf in a version matching the tree, which the runner does not
have; fetch-and-patch.sh touches the generated files for the same reason.

This is a platform patch, not a Turbo patch. It is not part of the reference
build because the reference build is Linux, where the libraries are real.

---
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -1022,8 +1022,11 @@
   # libtool.
   EXTRALDFLAGS="$EXTRALDFLAGS -all-static"
   dnl For non-MinGW build, we need additional libs for static build.
+  dnl
+  dnl iOS is Darwin: pthread, dlopen and clock_gettime all live in libSystem,
+  dnl and there is no separate librt, libdl or libpthread to link against.
   case "$host" in
-    *mingw*|*msvc*|*darwin*)
+    *mingw*|*msvc*|*darwin*|*ios*)
     ;;
 
     *)
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -28519,7 +28519,7 @@
   # libtool.
   EXTRALDFLAGS="$EXTRALDFLAGS -all-static"
     case "$host" in
-    *mingw*|*msvc*|*darwin*)
+    *mingw*|*msvc*|*darwin*|*ios*)
     ;;
 
     *)
